  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLIMATE ACTION FOR REDUCTION OF HUMANITARIAN NEEDS THROUGH RESILIENCE AGRICULTURE IN YOBE STATE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ajwad Humanitarian Initiative (AHI) is an NGO proposing to address climate-related risks, reduce external funding dependency, and strengthen community engagement. Through comprehensive capacity-building efforts, including training programs and knowledge transfer, the project entitled:  Climate Action for Reduction of Humanitarian Needs through Resilience Agriculture in Yobe State seeks to empower the local community to adapt to changing agro-climatic conditions. Additionally, the project incorporates market analysis and contingency plans to navigate potential challenges, fostering resilience and self-sufficiency within the community implementing a project that is benefiting 225 farming households.</narrative>
  </description>
